{"title":"Topicwise Test-5 Part Syllabus GATE 2026 DA Probability and Statistics-1","fileName":"069_Topicwise Test-5 Part Syllabus GATE 2026 DA Probability and Statistics-1.html","branch":"DATA SCIENCE AND ARTIFICIAL INTELLIGENCE","series":"GATE 2026 + GATE 2025 Online Test Series Data Science and AI","provider":"MADE EASY","duration":2700,"questions":[{"qnum":1,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":1,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>In a college’s mathematics department, there are 7 women and 9 men. How many distinct ways can a committee of 5 members be formed such that the committee includes atleast one women and atleast one men?</p></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"4221","high":"4221"},"solution":"<p>4221</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/3724187738387563f2c9515dd6fc148285594359.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":2,"type":"MCQ","correct":"B","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p>A company tested a new software with three types of uses : Beginner, Intermediate and Expert.<br />\nThe data collected is given below:</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/b631c5d16391884ba4b2735fa61274fce1f16d40.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>\n<div>A user is selected at random and is found to have report a bug. What is the probability that user is a Beginner.</div>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/3681dd793b1eae24eda7429eeb25f35c58701589.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/2843589ca66fded66c87f881d9a3c2ab7ba0927c.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/ae4b5cc8efff129bd19a45933a4b591fd2b8f35e.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/90c8e7596338c39644a6baa9fd2d3826d8328c25.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(b)</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/f743b454a7845537935fbb7641b442ef0af343e2.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":3,"type":"MCQ","correct":"B","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p>Let <em>A</em> and <em>B</em> be two non-empty events such that <em>P</em>(<em>A</em>) = <em>P</em><sub>1</sub>, <em>P</em>(<em>B</em>) = <em>P</em><sub>2</sub>.</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/cc057042bddaf66c9b4db0c7f746e28982952b18.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>\n<div>Which of the following statements is true?</div>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/e088de589d7fc408f306515bcb0a9729f724928b.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" />= <em>P</em><sub>1</sub> + <em>P</em><sub>2</sub> always valid when <em>A</em>, <em>B</em> are independent.</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> Y = 0 which contradicts independence.</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> Mutual exclusivity of <em>A</em> ∪ <em>B</em> and <em>A</em> ∩ <em>B</em> → <em>A</em> = <em>B</em>.</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> None of these</div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(b)</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/adaff0f5c3f6819d763b829f7af9bebe67393e9c.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>\n<div> </div>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":4,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":1,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>If A, B, C are mutually exclusive and exhaustive events associated with a random experiment and <em>P</em>(<em>B</em>) = 0.6 <em>P</em>(<em>A</em>) and <em>P</em>(<em>C</em>) = 0.2 <em>P</em>(<em>A</em>), then <em>P</em>(<em>A</em>) is _________. (Upto 2 decimal places)</p></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"0.55","high":"0.55"},"solution":"<p>0.55 [0.55 - 0.60]</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/130db78c45ccf5047c2b8f2d3b46022d3b5383ab.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":5,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":2,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>A six digit number is formed from 0 2 3 4 5 6 7 8 9. What is the probability that the number is divisible by 5 given that it is divisible by 4. (Repetition of digits is not allowed) (Rounded off answer to two decimal places)</p></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"0.36","high":"0.36"},"solution":"<p>0.36 [0.367 - 0.370]</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/bd611b5f7973400a94b6039d16f695a22a434f7c.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":6,"type":"MCQ","correct":"C","right":2,"wrong":0.66,"qtext":"<p>Let <em>X</em> be a continuous random variable representing the time (in hours) a machine operates before a failure.<br />\nThe probability density functions PDF) of <em>X</em> is given by</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/ec7d784a970d0143ae6540284ac3d48313bbcb33.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>\n<div> </div>\n<div>A machine is selected and it is known that the machine has failed with the first 20 hours of operation. What is the probability that the machine fails after 10 hours, given that it has failed within the first 20 hour? (Mark nearest option)</div>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> 0.231</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> 0.253</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> 0.270</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> 0.281</div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(c)</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/a2899e1dbac98c067e16ce2a761f03fbbaa89d68.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":7,"type":"MCQ","correct":"D","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p>Find the probability that a sum of 3 appears before a sum of 7 when rolling two fair dice repeatedly.</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/8722d59b3c356937f412783c7479e45557e29459.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/995ab8fcb4efc1d8419d3231e59caf29257a1925.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/4edd89824b7173364bd0eba97705f96b8f622393.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/05732bf8cf3c2609eb4059182ba816e39172f4ad.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","isCorrect":true}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(d)</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/5b1e074344da45e39e79f7cab5847f07ea418b80.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>\n<div> </div>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":8,"type":"MCQ","correct":"D","right":2,"wrong":0.66,"qtext":"<p>A vault has two destruct switches.<br />\n<em>X</em>(hidden) and <em>Y</em>(visible). Engineer obscure.<br />\n• The vault beeps normally (<em>Y</em> = 0) in two scenarios:<br />\n(i) 30% of the time with <em>X</em> disarmed (<em>X</em> = 0).<br />\n(ii) 45% of the time with <em>X</em> armed (<em>X</em> = 1).<br />\n• The vault blares alarms (<em>Y</em> = 1) otherwise.<br />\nDuring a drill, the vault beeps normally what’s the probability the vault was armed.</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> 0.45</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> 0.75</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> 0.65</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> 0.6</div>","isCorrect":true}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(d)</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/21b58050bb8d3bfaa86d40a25cbb60f960d2e195.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":9,"type":"MCQ","correct":"C","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p>Three fair coins are tossed. Given that atleast one tail has occurred, what is the probability that atmost one head has occurred?</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/c50b58dd03cc714f1193256e0e21e168f2c64772.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/113919501d693bc704b1d1a0c947992f307c74a0.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/e4d9d11de8434cacc45dc419a27d6aed146873b5.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/73833ec412a57e333d931366fd5db336069e016b.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(c)</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/86c94fd4a219886fd390076bbc62a0905658f86e.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":10,"type":"MCQ","correct":"B","right":2,"wrong":0.66,"qtext":"<p>Let the joint probability density function of a random variables <em>X</em> and <em>Y</em> be given by:</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/b43123f4f6c5672e0fd9a78ad39f4d26ea552522.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>\n<div>Calculate the probability <em>P</em>(1 < <img src=\"/media/51c1dc63b87a827a01b98ac07b15c64184b211b3.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /> < 2)</div>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/5ca5bda14ea21553f515dccb4eac377d007e1056.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/9bb03220598c096afa2a33349c9976cb288dd467.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/8b7604d96fe84f50ebc16d8d6a6112d4b3158658.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/5edcc174cb4dac6f68134ed1b0532f2d986eda0d.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(b)</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/f393f58f59728cd0d1826030231104cc938ca6ba.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>\n<div> </div>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":11,"type":"MCQ","correct":"D","right":2,"wrong":0.66,"qtext":"<p>Consider X and Y are two random independent events. It is known that <em>P</em>(<em>Y</em>) = 0.60 and <em>P</em>(<em>X</em><sup>C</sup> ∪ <em>Y</em>) = 0.80. Which one of the following is the value of <em>P</em>(<em>X</em> ∪ <em>Y</em>)?</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> 0.5</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> 0.6</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> 0.7</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> 0.8</div>","isCorrect":true}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(d)</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/2957c109a2a22244745df4c6ebb7d54f3086dd84.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":12,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":1,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>In how many different ways can 8 identical balls be distributed among three children if each receives at least two balls and no more than four balls ________?</p></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"6","high":"6"},"solution":"<p>6</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/ed9554894f9c4acafc7c7ccce0cf9e366f1d37dc.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":13,"type":"MCQ","correct":"A","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p>The joint probability mass function of <em>X</em> and <em>Y</em> is given in the table below:</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/4dcc6aed917be09a1243bfe0137cb983c93112f0.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>\n<div>What is the marginal probability <em>P</em>(<em>X</em> = 2)?</div>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> 0.5</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> 0.6</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> 0.45</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> 0.35</div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(a)</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/5be9b058822994c38090e8b4210d297aa97cd8f9.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":14,"type":"MCQ","correct":"C","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p>Suppose an algorithm process an input of size <em>n</em>, and in each of <em>n</em> steps, it select an index <img src=\"/media/8d41ce36102cc1eecf98dcd8ef7d7288ec1e9713.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /> ∈ {1, 2, ..., <em>n</em>} uniformly at random. Let <em>A</em> be the event that the index <img src=\"/media/c6238032d1fc7c7d9de744ef499d2446f7946384.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /> are never selected in any of the n steps.<br />\nAs <em>n</em> → ∞, what is the limiting value of the probability of event <em>A</em>?</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> 0</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/26d39d23ca0fbe9a9fa10d5a7a359139a510f1e3.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/5e8e83f287cf7261983d62ceb180b74ac9a5a155.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/b57ebad4c21c78bd59d7d9bbb0828ce8915f0f20.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(c)</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/dbdad11e4afe5032ea0617d7d5c166c610984687.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":15,"type":"MCQ","correct":"B","right":2,"wrong":0.66,"qtext":"<p>Let <em>X</em> and <em>Y</em> be continuous random variable with the joint probability density function given by</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/e4b02047c08a49f4ffce83527b128ba88e5be011.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>\n<div>Let <img src=\"/media/6f1c6d43a97005cc5de33ee1e9ca494768b3a7c6.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /> denoted the marginal probability of <em>X</em>, find the probability <img src=\"/media/b14080b4854db064e7be6f56242d25dff2d6e411.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/6d798a0944bb309069ca679b89dbb260466804e9.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/01a1ee128d243a85cbe43583aecdf0b72ead383a.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/203a8349241d2b3201e7116758b0379f4f6b7c9d.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/0563ce4a677ff8f8553abf8fab305690cde6ee54.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(b)</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/1b2dac1bf7b0e425b09d698f6bc01ffa340c158c.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":16,"type":"MCQ","correct":"D","right":2,"wrong":0.66,"qtext":"<p>The joint density function of <em>X</em> and <em>Y</em> is given by</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/703e53eae60056d2cf0e51814c9ae9517f6ebb26.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>\n<div>What is the probability <em>P</em>(<em>X</em> > 1, <em>Y</em> < 1)?</div>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/6661073f019a520b2d6a84ca1bfc1ea251fa1eb9.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/aaf5b9f6b59b3562c6839a1dde0878c4d10a58fb.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/181a4016575c03896848b687f279d43738fdaa0a.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/b2fecafea43e8e4834d6adb51c01d305a1eae949.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","isCorrect":true}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(d)</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/18c2e6e9b738182fe3002aabbebe97d0814e1100.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/dcc7a6d9d28db2ca84e50683a65f1796ab5e8ac6.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>\n<div> </div>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":17,"type":"MSQ","correct":"A,B,D","right":2,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>Let <em>A</em> and <em>B</em> be two events in a probability space with <em>P</em>(<em>A</em>) > 0 and <em>P</em>(<em>B</em>) > 0.<br />\nWhich of the following statements is/are necessarily true?</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> If <em>A</em> and <em>B</em> are independent, they cannot be mutually exclusive</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> If <em>A</em> and <em>B</em> are mutually exclusive, they cannot be independent.</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> If <em>A</em> and <em>B</em> are independent, then <em>P</em>(<em>A</em> ∪ <em>B</em>) = <em>P</em>(<em>A</em>) + <em>P</em>(<em>B</em>).</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> If <em>A</em> and <em>B</em> are mutually exclusive, then <em>P</em>(<em><u>A</u></em> ∩ <em>B<sup>C</sup></em>) = <em>P</em>(<em>A</em>).</div>","isCorrect":true}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(a, b, d)</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/1633a91b8a897342080754ccbb0909f8eafbdc96.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","subject":"Technical"}],"questionCount":17,"parsedAt":"2026-11-10T19:39:08.523Z"}